id: pm-c0lrdm
title: "Cross-harness provenance adapters: automatically resolve native model, version, and effort signals beyond Claude without identity flags"
description: "The bounded non-environment resolver shipped for Claude session JSONL and AI_AGENT_VERSION, but fresh Codex mutations on 2026-08-03 still record model null and effort null. The built-in registry covers seven harness names while live non-null provenance is effectively harness-specific. Build a public SDK adapter contract and privacy-reviewed built-in adapters for Codex, OpenCode, Pi, Cursor, Aider, and Gemini CLI. Each adapter declares its native sources, supported dimensions, bounded probe policy, normalization vocabulary, version, confidence, and explicit unavailable or failed outcomes. Packages may register adapters without patching CLI code. No agent supplies PM_AUTHOR or repeats model or thinking-level flags."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,"area:sdk",extensibility,identity,instrument-integrity,observability,provenance,security
created_at: "2026-08-03T11:08:43.782Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T11:15:48.164Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: "A versioned public SDK adapter interface declares harness detection, native sources, supported dimensions, bounded probe limits, normalization, source attribution, and explicit outcome categories; Built-in adapters cover Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode, Pi, Cursor, Aider, and Gemini CLI; each adapter has a redacted real boundary fixture or a documented no-signal waiver; A live Codex mutation records the actual model family and reasoning effort available to the harness, without PM_AUTHOR, author, model, or effort flags; if the platform exposes neither, the exact unavailable source is observable rather than silently null; Probe implementations read only allow-listed metadata fields under byte and time ceilings, fail closed, never block a mutation, never retain arbitrary session text or host paths, and can be disabled by policy; CLI, SDK, MCP, extension, nested-process, npx, and bunx paths share the same adapter result and immutable source attribution; Packages can add or override a harness adapter through the SDK registry with schema validation, priority rules, collision diagnostics, and no CLI source change; Corpus coverage reports success, unavailable, failed, and undeclared rates per harness and dimension; a negative control proves CI fails when a declared live adapter remains inert; Normalization preserves raw provider identifiers only when policy permits and always emits a stable model-family and effort vocabulary suitable for longitudinal analytics"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Record trustworthy harness, model, version, and reasoning-effort provenance automatically across the supported agent fleet"
value: Attribution and quality analytics become comparable across harnesses instead of being accurate only for the first implemented adapter
impact: "Enables model-aware context, cost, throughput, evaluation, and defect-escape analysis while eliminating manual author configuration"
outcome: "Every supported harness either records its native identity dimensions with an attributable source or a precise, observable unavailable or failed reason"
why_now: "The current Codex session is correctly detected as a harness and unique instance, yet all four provenance dimensions are null; the closed Claude probe does not satisfy the cross-harness mandate"
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: high
confidence: medium
